      "channelName": "💬-discussion",
      "summary": "This Discord segment captures a community in crisis following Shaw's announcement that the Eliza token project is effectively dead. Shaw revealed that the project was sued by token holders, resulting in the complete depletion of the Eliza fund used to pay settlements. He stated there is no treasury, he owns no tokens, and the foundation support system is gone, advising token-focused members to leave. The community response was mixed - some members expressed anger and accusations of scamming, while others attempted constructive dialogue. Key technical points discussed include: the existing token infrastructure (DEX/CEX listings, CCIP integration, tokenomics with 607M tokens for liquidity, 275M for Protocol-Owned Liquidity, team vesting with 12-month cliff and 24-month linear schedule, SAFT allocations in locked multisig). Zadayos proposed a separation model where Shaw could focus on open-source elizaos development while a separate entity handles commercialization and token operations, generating revenue through IP licensing, equity, royalties, development contracts, cloud fees, and enterprise support. The token had dropped 20% in one day following Shaw's sell advice, with market cap falling to $2M. Community members noted that Shaw had previously promoted a token migration and promised product launches, but failed to deliver utility. Xeno_thales argued that tokens cannot be killed and future Eliza products could revive token value. The discussion revealed deep frustration over lack of communication, with paolin_62616 noting 10 months without proper updates and questioning Shaw's leadership decisions. Multiple members referenced Shaw's history of launching and abandoning tokens, with accusations of deliberate deception regarding token utility and the Binance Alpha airdrop strategy that created artificial volume while holders sold immediately.",
